\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The saints of God, their conflicts past,
\par And life's long battle won at last,
\par No more they need the shield or sword;
\par They cast them down before their Lord:
\par O happy saints! For ever blest,
\par At Jesu's feet how safe their rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The saints of God, their wanderings done,
\par No more their weary course they run,
\par No more they faint, no more they fall,
\par No foes oppress, no fears appal:
\par O happy saints! For ever blest,
\par In that dear home, how sweet their rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The saints of God, life is voyage o'er,
\par Safe landed on that blissful shore,
\par No stormy tempests now they dread,
\par No roaring billows lift their head:
\par O happy saints! For ever blest,
\par In that calm haven of their rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.
\par O God of saints, to Thee we cry;
\par O Saviour, plead for us on high;
\par O Holy Ghost, our Guide and Friend,
\par Grant us Thy grace till life shall end:
\par That with all saints our rest may be
\par In that bright paradise with Thee.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

